  "card": "Expands compressed IPv6 addresses into full eight-group notation when sending destination hostnames in SOCKS5 CONNECT requests. Outbound connections through Tor SOCKS5 proxies fail with a general failure error for peers whose IPv6 addresses contain an inner double colon, because Tor exit relays mistakenly parse the combined address and port string as an eight-group IPv6 address with no port. The author notes this affects approximately 20% of IPv6 addresses in addrman and 29% of DNS seed IPv6 answers, with no fallback to direct connections. Mainnet testing against Tor 0.4.9.13 confirmed four seed peers that previously failed with 30 connection errors were able to connect and complete handshakes with this fix.",
